@*
===========================================================
ORANGE TENDER MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
PAGE: My Purchase Requests

DEVELOPER OWNER: Doulat
MODULE: Department / Purchase Requests
TRELLO TASK: My Purchase Requests
TRELLO URL: https://trello.com/c/SjSwbYUx

PURPOSE:
List the department’s purchase requests with status and the
latest Sourcing Officer decision.

BUSINESS ACCESS:
Requesting Department (own department only)

ROUTE: /Department/PurchaseRequests

FUTURE IMPLEMENTATION:
- Query PurchaseRequests where DepartmentId = the user’s
  department.
- Show the latest PurchaseRequestReview decision and
  comment.
- Row actions: Details; Edit & resubmit for Draft/Returned.

DEPENDENCIES:
PurchaseRequests, PurchaseRequestReviews, Departments.

STATUS:
UI SCAFFOLD ONLY — BUSINESS LOGIC NOT IMPLEMENTED.
===========================================================
*@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "My Purchase Requests";
    ViewData["WorkspaceSection"] = "My Requests";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Purchase requests created by your department, with their review status.";
}
<partial name="_PageHeader" />
<partial name="_ScaffoldNotice" />

<section class="pg-toolbar" aria-label="Search and filters">
    <input type="search" placeholder="Search by title or reference" aria-label="Search by title or reference" disabled />
    <select aria-label="Status" disabled><option>Status: All</option><option>Status: Draft</option><option>Status: Submitted</option><option>Status: Returned</option><option>Status: Rejected</option><option>Status: Accepted</option></select>
    <select aria-label="Priority" disabled><option>Priority: All</option><option>Priority: Low</option><option>Priority: Normal</option><option>Priority: High</option><option>Priority: Urgent</option></select>
    <span class="pg-hint">Search and filters are not implemented yet.</span>
</section>

<section class="ws-panel pg-panel" aria-labelledby="tbl-purchase-requests">
    <div class="pg-panel-head"><h2 id="tbl-purchase-requests">Purchase requests</h2><a class="pg-btn pg-btn-primary" asp-area="Department" asp-controller="PurchaseRequests" asp-action="Create">New request</a></div>
    <div class="pg-table-wrap">
        <table class="pg-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Reference</th><th scope="col">Title</th><th scope="col">Priority</th><th scope="col">Needed by</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Last submitted</th><th scope="col">Actions</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody><tr><td colspan="7"><partial name="_EmptyState" model='"Your department has no purchase requests yet."' /></td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<aside class="pg-note"><strong>Returned requests</strong><p>A request returned by the Sourcing Officer shows the Officer’s comment. Edit and resubmit it; every submission is kept in PurchaseRequestReviews.</p></aside>
